      "name": "Open interactive shell via Ebury backdoor commands",
      "description": "Get an interactive Unix shell on a compromised Linux server, at the backdoor's or at root's privilege level. The operator sends the custom command Xcsh or Xcls to the trojanized OpenSSH process for a shell with Ebury-level permissions, or Xxsh for a root shell; the backdoored keyutils shared library loaded by OpenSSH handles the commands. Published by MITRE ATT&CK as a procedure example of Ebury (S0377) for T1059.004.",
      "platforms": [
        "Linux"
      ],
      "tactics": [
        "execution"
      ],
      "x_technique_refs": [
        "attack-pattern--a9d4b653-6915-42af-98b2-5758c4ceee56"
      ],
